  zukan_caution: "Never apply undiluted essential oil directly to the skin, and never ingest it. If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, an infant, or living with a medical condition, consult a professional such as a doctor or pharmacist before use. See “Learning Safely” on the top page for details.",
  wa_h: "Feature — Wa-Seiyu (Japanese Oils)", wa_badge: "FEATURE",
  wa_h3: "Learn the scents of Japan's forests and satoyama.",
  wa_lead: "Wa-seiyu is the collective name for essential oils obtained from plants grown in Japan. Yuzu floated in the bath, the woody scent of hinoki, kuromoji — long known as a Japanese aromatic wood — and hakka, which passes crisply through the nose: the plants that have stood beside daily life in this country take the starring role as scents. This feature studies the representative wa-seiyu from three angles — producing regions and satoyama, the craft of distillation, and scenes of daily life.",
  wa_p1t: "Regions & satoyama", wa_p1: "Scents tied to their places of origin — yuzu from Kochi, hinoki from Shikoku and Yoshino, hakka from Kitami, Hokkaido, and more",
